<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jena</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jena is a university city on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saale">Saale</a> river in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thuringia">Thuringia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Its university, founded in 1558, made it a centre of German philosophy and literature around 1800. On 14 October 1806 <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> defeated the Prussians near the city at the Battle of Jena. From the nineteenth century Carl <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carl-zeiss-ag">Zeiss</a> and Otto Schott made Jena a centre of the optical and glass industries.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jena.jpg" alt="Jena" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Henry Mühlpfordt · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Zentrum_Jenas_im_Tal_2008-05-24.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
